From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-16
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 031] panvk: v9 JM: decode BC images leaving ZERO_INITIALIZED biblioklept

The BC decode of images leaving VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_ZERO_INITIALIZED_EXT
(csf-v11/040, cmd_bc_decode_zero_initialized()) was only called from the
CSF CmdPipelineBarrier2. On the v9 JM backend such an image sampled the
zeroed decoded plane instead of the decode of zero blocks (opaque black
for BC1).

v9 is on the same path as the CSF parts that already work:
- textureCompressionBC comes from panvk_bc_emul_enabled(), which looks
  at the native mask, not the arch (csf-v11/108; G57 reports BC1-BC3
  only, so it emulates).
- image->bc_gfx needs pan_arch >= 10, so v9 always uses the compute
  decode into the decoded plane after the raw blocks, as v6/v7 do.
- VK_EXT_zero_initialize_device_memory and the ZERO_INITIALIZED layout
  are exposed for every arch (zeroInitializeDeviceMemory = true, the
  layout is listed for host image copy).
- The JM barrier already closes the batch and opens a new one. The
  decode records its internal barrier through CmdPipelineBarrier2 with
  memory barriers only, so it does not recurse.

The call is added for all JM arches (v6, v7, v9) without a PAN_ARCH
gate. jm-v7-wip/0013 adds the same call for PAN_ARCH < 9 only and is now
redundant with this.

Build-only; not device-tested.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
index b7845ed..86b5ce8 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -443,6 +443,13 @@ panvk_per_arch(CmdPipelineBarrier2)(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
       panvk_per_arch(cmd_close_batch)(cmdbuf);
       panvk_per_arch(cmd_open_batch)(cmdbuf);
    }
+
+   /* BC emulation: an image leaving VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_ZERO_INITIALIZED_EXT
+    * has zero blocks, whose decoded texels are not zero (BC1 decodes them
+    * to opaque black). Decode them as CSF does. The internal barriers it
+    * records have no image barriers, so this does not recurse.
+    */
+   panvk_per_arch(cmd_bc_decode_zero_initialized)(cmdbuf, pDependencyInfo);
 }
 
 static void
